Description:

cyr_deny -r marks a user replica-only; use it rather than creating the
file under replicaonly/ by hand, because it takes the user's lock, so no
writer can proceed once it returns.  Local changes to replica-only data (a
marked user, or anything on a server with replicaonly set) are now refused
with an error rather than aborting the process: IMAP writes get NO
[UNAVAILABLE], JMAP writes get serverUnavailable, DAV writes get a 503,
and delivery gets a 4.2.1 tempfail.  On replicas, cyr_expire cleans up
expunged messages but leaves expiry and the removal of deleted (DELETED.*)
mailboxes to the master.

Two new login policies.  auth_userexists refuses a login when the user's
INBOX does not exist or has been deleted.  auth_notreplicaonly refuses a
login when the server, or the user, is replica-only.  Logins as an admin
and anonymous logins are exempt from both.


Documentation:

imapd.conf(5), cyr_deny(8)


Config changes:

auth_userexists, auth_notreplicaonly


Upgrade instructions:

On a server with replicaonly set, clients that could previously make local
changes (which then diverged from the master) now get errors instead.
auth_userexists and auth_notreplicaonly default to off.


